cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  LUCID-PD: a leakage-controlled clinical decision support prototype for
  Parkinson's disease
message: If you use this software or its findings, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Eyo
    given-names: Nkese
    affiliation: Coventry University
repository-code: https://github.com/nkeseeyo/lucid-pd-cdss
abstract: >-
  A clinical decision support prototype for Parkinson's disease that treats
  validation protocol as the object of study. It detects Parkinson's from
  sustained-vowel speech under subject-level cross-validation, explains each
  decision with SHAP attribution and retrieval-grounded text, routes the result
  through auditable rules, and reproduces the widely reported MRI convolutional
  baseline to quantify how much of its accuracy is an artefact of splitting
  images rather than scans.
keywords:
  - Parkinson's disease
  - clinical decision support
  - data leakage
  - subject-level validation
  - explainable artificial intelligence
  - speech processing
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
